    "hypothesis": "Combining static OpenMP work-sharing across independent columns with a linear run-count mode scan should reduce full-program time while preserving each column's arithmetic and the required seven output lines. A pairwise fallback retains mode behavior when NaNs disrupt sorting.",
    "notes": "The parallel guard retains the generic rows-squared-by-columns estimate for the unchanged bubble sort and computes the threshold without multiplication overflow. The controller should measure this combined candidate; no timing is claimed here.",
